text Our peaceful days continue on.
text I think that as long as I'm here with her, they'll never end.
text I think that even if we're the only two alive in this world, they'll never stop.
text But something has begun to change...
text ...with winter's arrival.
text It's as if winter... is trying to steal away her energy.
text As the temperature drops, she begins to sleep more.
text The two of us used to always be so lively when we played together.
text Far in the distance, I see ominous clouds filling the sky.
text ...Snow clouds, no doubt.
text I realize that now is the time to decide.
text If I don't now, it'll all be too late.
text I feel as though we still have time.
text Once winter comes, everything will be buried in snow.
text We need to act before that time comes.
setvar strS[1000] = "BG301"
setvar intA[1000] = 1
if intA[1000] == 0
	goto s45
fi
goto 46
label s45
setvar strS[1000] = ""
label 46
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 98
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
text When I return to our cabin, she's sitting down, leaning against the wall and blankly looking out the window.
text The sight worries me.
text Is it all because of the cold?
text I approach her and point out the window.
text I point to a place farther than where she's looking. To the edge of the sky.
text ..."Hm?"
text She notices what I'm doing and looks at me.
text ..."What about that place?"
text I continue to point.
text ..."Do you want to go there?"
text Another nod.
text ..."But winter is coming."
text I continue to stare into her face.
text ..."You still want to?"
text Another nod.
text ..."If it gets any colder, I won't be able to move..."
text Then now's the time.
text ..."And also, if we leave this house, we won't be able to come back..."
text ......
text ..."You still want to?"
text I nod again.
text ..."What's over there?"
text I hop up and down.
text ..."Something fun?"
text One more nod.
text ..."A place full of things to do..."
text ..."Where every day is fun..."
text ..."And it's always warm...?"
text I nod vigorously.
text ..."But we won't be able to make it in time..."
text ..."The winter clouds will catch up to us..."
text I search my memories.
text The deep, murky swamp that is my memory bank.
text The sky.
text We need to go to the sky.
text I motion upward.
text ..."We're going... to the sky?"
text I nod vigorously.
text ..."How?"
text I take her hand.
text ..."We're going to make it?"
text I nod vigorously again.
text ..."A vehicle that can... fly through the sky?"
text Another nod.
text I can see exactly what it should look like inside my heart.
text Is it getting across and reaching her...?
text ......
text After she stares blankly for another brief period...
text She gives me a little nod of her own this time.
setvar strS[1000] = "KURO"
