text I gather junk, and she puts it together.
text The sky grows more and more cloudy.
text I look up at the mountains as they come together.
text I imagine large wings growing from them.
text Please, before winter comes...
text Let us be in the sky, flying with those wings.
text The breaths she exhales are white.
text She wipes her eyes.
text ..."I'm a little sleepy."
text I look up at her, worried.
text ..."Sorry, let's keep going."
text She continues to work hard.
text Perhaps she understands too.
text She knows what we have to do right now.
text She even said it herself:
text If winter comes, she won't be able to move.
text I don't quite understand what she meant by that.
text But I think she meant she'll be powerless to do anything.
text So we continue to work, never stopping for a break.
text I keep bringing junk to her as well.
